Ben, I wanted to talk to you about school.

250
00:14:40,060 --> 00:14:41,080
What about it?

251
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:48,280
Ben... What you've learned in these two weeks has made me so proud.

252
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:52,580
What would you say if, uh, you didn't have to go back to school?

253
00:14:53,420 --> 00:14:55,160
You mean I learned so much I graduated?

254
00:14:57,340 --> 00:15:01,800
No, Ben, I'm saying that you have done better in these two weeks than you have ever

255
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:03,340
done at Dewey.

256
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:08,420
And how would you feel about just going to school here at home?

257
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,540
Mom, this isn't funny.

258
00:15:12,820 --> 00:15:16,260
Ben, I saw you actually excited about doing schoolwork.

259
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:18,700
I mean, you and I had fun together.

260
00:15:18,820 --> 00:15:22,120
Shh! Mom, if my friends heard you say that, they'd laugh at me.

261
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:24,780
You know what they're gonna do when they find out I'm going to Mommy High?

262
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,240
I got you.

263
00:15:28,700 --> 00:15:30,940
Honey, I really think it's for the best.

264
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:33,700
And underneath, I think you do, too.

265
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:37,960
I mean, can you honestly tell me, can you honestly say that you can hang out with

266
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:40,140
Vito and the Coconut Boys and not get into trouble?

267
00:15:42,140 --> 00:15:44,140
I certainly... I most certainly can't...

268
00:15:45,880 --> 00:15:47,920
So this is what I get for my two weeks of hard work.

269
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:50,440
More punishment? Ben, when you're older, you'll understand.

270
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:52,140
I won't be getting any older.

271
00:15:52,260 --> 00:15:53,660
Mama's boys have a short lifespan.

272
00:15:59,460 --> 00:16:01,080
I see you took the news well.

273
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:08,320
Jason, I firmly believe that underneath, deep, deep, deep within his soul, he knows

274
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:09,040
this is for the best.

275
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:10,920
I don't know, Maggie.

276
00:16:10,980 --> 00:16:14,420
I mean, when I was his age, all I cared about was snapping towels with the guys and

277
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:17,720
smelling bad and getting all goofy and nervous around females.

278
00:16:18,400 --> 00:16:20,280
That happened when you were younger, too?

279
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:24,140
There's no need to lash out at me, Maggie.

280
00:16:24,180 --> 00:16:24,840
Yes, there is.

281
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,860
Jason, I don't feel like I have your support in this.

282
00:16:27,060 --> 00:16:30,220
Honey, look, I mean, all things considered, when you look at the options,

283
00:16:31,680 --> 00:16:34,700
I think teaching Ben at home is worth a shot.

284
00:16:36,220 --> 00:16:41,640
But if you want me to say that what you're doing is absolutely 100%, no doubt about

285
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:45,720
it, right. I can't say that unless you want me to lie.

286
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:48,580
Would it be a big lie?

287
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:53,500
How can you forget that Los Angeles is in California?

288
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:56,920
It is the corporate headquarters of Leilani's Luau on a stick.

289
00:16:58,980 --> 00:17:01,220
Uh, Mother? Oh, word.

290
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:07,300
You hurt, don't you?

291
00:17:07,940 --> 00:17:13,140
No. Mom, this is me, Carol, your sensitive, perceptive daughter.

292
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:14,860
Mom, it's okay.

293
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:19,360
I know why you're going through this pointless charade, to make up for the tragedy

294
00:17:19,360 --> 00:17:20,740
of those lost years.

295
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:22,360
But it's okay.

296
00:17:22,900 --> 00:17:26,100
Guilt has made women far better than you go insane.

297
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:33,200
Listen, you rocks, because of you, she's gonna wanna try this on me.

298
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:35,440
There goes my socialization.

299
00:17:37,460 --> 00:17:40,900
Look I'm not too happy about this either the last place I want to be is here

300
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:44,520
Then do something about it run away from home.

301
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:46,080
I'll pack your clothes for you

302
00:17:47,820 --> 00:17:51,180
Everything you miss today covered in your homework and you will stay in your room

303
00:17:51,180 --> 00:17:55,120
until you know it backwards and forwards or you will rot Like a bad melon and that

304
00:17:55,120 --> 00:18:00,260
is a simile you could take to the bank

305
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:05,020
Mrs. Seaver I could hear you a block away

306
00:18:06,380 --> 00:18:08,460
You know, you would have made a great teacher.

307
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:14,160
Mr. DeWitt, if you have come here to tell me that Ben needs socialization, or that

308
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:18,220
he needs to hang out with boys or snap towels or act goofy around females, or that I

309
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:20,540
am doing this only out of guilt, save it.

310
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:21,480
I have heard it all.

311
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:23,920
Here. Here, teach.

312
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:30,000
What? Mrs. Siever, I have come here to applaud you.

313
00:18:30,920 --> 00:18:37,240
Uh... For the first time in my career, I have seen a parent do something right.

314
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:41,040
You took control of your son's life when he needed it the most.

315
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,400
Wow, well, thanks.

316
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:45,820
It was just when I was beginning to doubt myself.

317
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:52,240
All I can say is I just wish that all the parents of all the students in all the

318
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:56,700
classrooms around the world would take them home and teach them.

319
00:18:59,520 --> 00:19:01,360
But then you'd be out of a job.

320
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:03,100
I'm a city employee.

321
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:04,480
I ain't going nowhere.

322
00:19:06,960 --> 00:19:12,000
On the QT, my mommy taught me at home for 14 years, and look how I turned out.

323
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:20,120
Um, Mom, I'm too sick to stay home today.

324
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:20,940
I gotta go to school.

325
00:19:23,900 --> 00:19:25,720
Ben, don't... It's okay, honey.

326
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:28,360
Go. You're not arguing?

327
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:32,020
No. It was a mistake teaching you at home.

328
00:19:32,140 --> 00:19:33,580
I'm sorry I ever got into it.

329
00:19:34,100 --> 00:19:35,140
How could you say that?

330
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:36,400
Come on, I was doing good, wasn't I?

331
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:37,380
Ben, just go to school.

332
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:38,080
You're gonna be late.

333
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:39,180
I don't want to go to school.

334
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:40,360
Oh, so now you want him to stay home?

335
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:41,320
I didn't say that either.

336
00:19:41,580 --> 00:19:43,340
Well, Ben, those are your two choices.

337
00:19:43,740 --> 00:19:44,440
Make up your mind.

338
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:44,980
Yeah, I know.

339
00:19:44,980 --> 00:19:46,060
It's driving me nuts.

340
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:55,600
What is? Mom, I like studying with you.

341
00:19:55,980 --> 00:19:57,440
And I actually learned something.

342
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:01,940
I mean, it's not real neat having everybody calling you stupid.

343
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:04,620
Who calls you stupid?

344
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:06,580
It's my image.

345
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:08,000
I mean, it's what I do.

346
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:08,820
It's what I am.

347
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:10,680
I don't like that.

348
00:20:10,880 --> 00:20:12,820
Yeah, I don't like it either.

349
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:15,660
But you know, I'll tell you what's worse.

350
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:18,020
It's having all those guys call me a mama's boy.

351
00:20:19,040 --> 00:20:20,000
Who's saying that?

352
00:20:20,580 --> 00:20:21,480
They all are, Mom.

353
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:27,340
When they walk by the house dragging their battle on the fence, they're saying it.

354
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:31,720
When I hear tires squeal late at night, it's meant for me, Mom.

355
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,120
I just don't know what to do.

356
00:20:35,060 --> 00:20:37,660
I mean, it's really neat having you all to myself.

357
00:20:39,040 --> 00:20:40,860
It's really neat not feeling dumb.

358
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:45,540
You did like being here with me?

359
00:20:45,820 --> 00:20:48,400
Shh! Come on.

360
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,000
They could show up at any time.

361
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:51,460
They've been known to hide in bushes.

362
00:20:53,900 --> 00:20:56,480
Well, you are more trouble than you're worth, young man.

363
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:59,100
Huh? You are too dangerous for public school.

364
00:20:59,140 --> 00:21:00,860
You can just tell your friends I said so.

365
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:02,400
I'm not dangerous.

366
00:21:03,200 --> 00:21:05,640
Such things wouldn't be said about a mama's boy, would they?

367
00:21:06,460 --> 00:21:11,820
No. Oh, so I could, like, go to school here and nobody would have to know that I'm

368
00:21:11,820 --> 00:21:12,700
actually liking it?

369
00:21:12,740 --> 00:21:13,640
That's right, honey.

370
00:21:13,860 --> 00:21:18,760
Honey? I mean, deadbeat, you are too wild to be let loose on the streets.

371
00:21:20,220 --> 00:21:24,800
You're welcome. This isn't gonna be any picnic, young man!

372
00:21:27,260 --> 00:21:29,340
Are we still acting or should I be worried?

373
00:21:35,360 --> 00:21:38,320
Mom, how come you had to go back to work?

374
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:40,200
I didn't have to, Ben.

375
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:42,380
I wanted to.

376
00:21:44,540 --> 00:21:52,700
Come here. Ben, imagine you had to spend 15 years in this house without ever going

377
00:21:52,700 --> 00:21:53,360
out to play.

378
00:21:53,900 --> 00:21:55,440
You'd go crazy, wouldn't you?

379
00:21:55,900 --> 00:22:00,320
Mm -hmm. Well, believe it or not, a lot of grown -ups feel the same way about work.

380
00:22:01,140 --> 00:22:02,260
That's sick, Mom.

381
00:22:04,260 --> 00:22:09,220
Ben, I know this has been a big change for all of us, and I worry about not being

382
00:22:09,220 --> 00:22:12,260
here for you because, well, you're the youngest.

383
00:22:13,100 --> 00:22:17,080
And I worry about not being here for Carol because she's a girl and she needs her

384
00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:21,640
mother. And I worry about not being here for Mike to keep him from accidentally

385
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:22,880
blowing something up.

386
00:22:24,180 --> 00:22:27,720
And believe me, I worry about leaving your father here to cope with all you

387
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:31,580
monsters. You shouldn't worry so much, Mom.

388
00:22:31,860 --> 00:22:33,320
You'll make yourself crazy.

389
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:47,260
MUSIC
